#X obj 674 11 data.fifo;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 426 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A FIFO (First In \, First Out) queue container. Values
are pushed to the back of the queue and popped from the front \, so
they are output in the same order in which they arrived. If the size
argument is specified \, the queue has a fixed size: when the number
of values exceeds this limit \, the oldest value is output and removed
to make room for the new one.;
#X text 240 199 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 224 • Event queue for algorithmic composition — accumulating
notes or triggers that will be processed later in the correct order
(first in \, first out).;
#X text 250 279 • Delaying a stream of values — every incoming value
is pushed into the queue \, and a later bang or clock pops them one
by one \, effectively delaying the stream by a fixed number of steps.;
#X text 250 349 • Buffer for real-time data — collecting sensor or
control values at one rate and reading them out at another \, for example
smoothing a jittery input stream.;
#X text 250 404 • Fixed-size history window — with the SIZE argument
set \, the queue keeps only the last N values. Older values are automatically
dropped \, which is useful for moving-average filters \, rolling statistics
\, or keeping a short history of recent events.;
